{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "U1: Treat the NPE as a Sqoop-Teradata integration defect; root-cause it inside the Spring XD launcher and, if the bug is in Sqoop's GenericJdbcManager, wrap the job with a TeradataConnManager shim that replicates the behavior of the Hortonworks connector, avoiding a Sqoop fork.",
    "U2: Externalize the log directory through a new configuration property (e.g. xd.log.dir) that defaults to ${xd.home}/logs, allowing it to be overridden via system property, environment variable, or xd.config.yml. Update Logback configuration to resolve the new property.",
    "U3: Carve out a new Maven module (spring-bus/message-bus) with its own release cadence; Spring XD will pull it as a dependency. Maintain binary compatibility by keeping the existing public API and moving tests verbatim.",
    "U4: Move the conversion service to spring-cloud-dataflow and expose a ModuleTypeConversion SPI so custom modules can register converters. Spring XD will consume the new library and provide default conversions for built-in payload types.",
    "U5: Reuse the same spring-bus repository created for U3. Add a new spring-bus/codec module that houses codec interfaces and built-in implementations (e.g. JSON, Java serialization, Kryo).",
    "U6: Implement SinglenodeAdmin as a thin ModuleLauncher that delegates to an in-process container instead of SSH/Container. It will reuse the existing XD Admin REST endpoints to maximize re-use of the admin UI and shell.",
    "U7: Build a Diego-based Admin SPI implementation on top of the Receptor API (Diego's task execution endpoint). Modules will be packaged as CF Diego droplets and submitted via Receptor; the implementation will follow the existing ModuleLauncher SPI so it is plug-compatible with the singlenode impl.",
    "U8: Scope the work as a time-boxed investigation spike. Evaluate Eureka, Consul, and Spring Cloud Services self-registration patterns. Produce a written design proposal with a recommended approach and, if time allows, a minimal POC in a sandbox project."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The developer is already familiar with Spring XD, Sqoop internals, Maven multi-module projects, and Cloud Foundry Diego/Receptor concepts, so no ramp-up/training time is included.",
    "A Teradata Express instance (or a JDBC-test stub) and Hortonworks Teradata connector JAR are available locally for reproducing and verifying the U1 fix.",
    "spring-bus (U3, U5) and spring-cloud-dataflow (U4) are existing or concurrently created repositories with their own build pipelines; coordinating repo creation is excluded from this estimate.",
    "CF Diego with the Receptor API is available in a test environment for U7; otherwise testing is limited to integration tests against a Diego in-process emulator.",
    "The Hortonworks Teradata connector licensing permits redistribution of the minimal shim layer if required.",
    "Standard development environment and tooling (JDK 17+, Maven 3.8+, IntelliJ, Git) are already provisioned.",
    "No major upstream Sqoop redesign is required for U1; the fix is contained in Spring XD launcher / connection-manager selection logic.",
    "All refactoring activities (U3, U4, U5) preserve existing public APIs to avoid breaking consumers outside Spring XD.",
    "U8 is a research/POC spike - it does not include production hardening or full feature implementation."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Investigate Sqoop-Teradata NPE",
      "activity_description": "Reproduce the NPE with the stock Teradata JDBC driver, trace the failure through Sqoop's JobBase / ConnManager code, and identify the missing/required connection-manager logic.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Implement Sqoop-Teradata fix",
      "activity_description": "Update the Spring XD Sqoop batch job to detect Teradata JDBC URLs and use a TeradataConnManager shim, or apply the smallest code change that avoids the NPE. Include unit tests for both driver and connection-manager selection paths.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Externalize logging directory",
      "activity_description": "Introduce xd.log.dir configuration property, update Logback configuration files, refactor code that hardcodes ${xd.home}/logs, and add documentation. Includes verification on an RPM-style install layout.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Move message-bus - analysis",
      "activity_description": "Catalog message-bus classes, dependencies, tests, and external callers; design the new spring-bus module structure and Maven coordinates; coordinate with spring-bus maintainers on package relocation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Move message-bus - implementation",
      "activity_description": "Relocate source/test/resources into the new spring-bus module, update package imports across Spring XD, switch XD's pom to depend on spring-bus, and fix the resulting compile errors.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Move message-bus - test & verify",
      "activity_description": "Run the relocated test suite in spring-bus, re-run XD integration tests, fix regressions caused by relocation, and update CI pipelines.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Move type conversion - analysis",
      "activity_description": "Identify all type-conversion classes, integration points with the XD module loader, and extension points needed to support custom modules. Coordinate with spring-cloud-dataflow team on the new ModuleTypeConversion SPI.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Move type conversion - implementation",
      "activity_description": "Relocate conversion code to spring-cloud-dataflow, define and implement the ModuleTypeConversion SPI, and update Spring XD to consume the new module and to register its built-in converters.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Add custom module type-conversion hook",
      "activity_description": "Implement a sample custom module demonstrating producer/consumer of a custom domain object, exposing the new SPI so users can plug in their own converters.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Move type conversion - test & verify",
      "activity_description": "Run relocated unit tests, exercise the custom-module sample end-to-end through an XD stream definition, and validate backward compatibility with existing modules.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Move serialization codec - analysis",
      "activity_description": "Inventory serialization codec classes (codec interfaces, built-in implementations, configuration metadata) and assess overlap with message-bus relocation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Move serialization codec - implementation",
      "activity_description": "Create spring-bus/codec module, relocate codec code, refactor XD references, and update Maven dependencies.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "Move serialization codec - test & verify",
      "activity_description": "Run codec unit tests in the new module and verify that streams defined in Spring XD still round-trip payloads with each supported codec.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "Singlenode Admin SPI - design",
      "activity_description": "Design the SinglenodeAdmin implementation, including in-process module launcher, container bootstrap, and how it will integrate with the existing XD Admin REST API.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A15",
      "activity_name": "Singlenode Admin SPI - implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement SinglenodeAdmin and the in-process ModuleLauncher, including module deploy/undeploy lifecycle, status tracking, and integration with the existing admin endpoints.",
      "most_likely_effort": 28
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A16",
      "activity_name": "Singlenode Admin SPI - test & verify",
      "activity_description": "Write integration tests that deploy representative stream and job definitions in the single-JVM mode, validate the admin UI/shell commands, and document usage.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A17",
      "activity_name": "Diego Receptor Admin - research",
      "activity_description": "Study CF Diego architecture, the Receptor API, task lifecycle, and how it differs from the existing SSH-based container launcher. Document findings and design choices.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A18",
      "activity_name": "Diego Receptor Admin - design",
      "activity_description": "Design the DiegoModuleLauncher and DiegoAdmin implementations, including droplet preparation, task submission, log retrieval, and status mapping to the XD module model.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A19",
      "activity_name": "Diego Receptor Admin - implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement DiegoModuleLauncher, DiegoAdmin, and supporting classes; integrate with the existing XD Admin SPI; add configuration for Diego target, org, space, and credentials.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A20",
      "activity_name": "Diego Receptor Admin - test & verify",
      "activity_description": "Integration-test deploying a stream to a CF Lattice/Diego environment, verifying module lifecycle, log streaming, and failure handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A21",
      "activity_name": "s-c-s self-registration investigation",
      "activity_description": "Survey existing self-registration patterns in Spring Cloud Services and related projects, evaluate feasibility for s-c-s modules, document trade-offs, and propose a recommended approach.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A22",
      "activity_name": "s-c-s self-registration POC",
      "activity_description": "Build a minimal proof-of-concept where a sample s-c-s module registers with a service registry (Eureka/Consul) and is discovered and orchestrated by an XD runtime on CF.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A23",
      "activity_name": "Build, CI, and release updates",
      "activity_description": "Update parent POMs, dependency management, and CI pipelines to reflect the new spring-bus and spring-cloud-dataflow dependencies and the relocated modules.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A24",
      "activity_name": "End-to-end integration & smoke testing",
      "activity_description": "Run a full Spring XD build with the relocated modules, execute smoke tests for streams/jobs, and verify admin/UI behavior across singlenode and Diego modes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A25",
      "activity_name": "Documentation updates",
      "activity_description": "Update reference docs, release notes, and migration notes covering the new logging configuration, module moves, and the two new Admin SPI implementations.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 294
  }
}
